<pdd-dependency>brain/collection_registry_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

% Goal

Maintain `brain/library_index.py` as the schema and sole active-index resolution boundary for all collection-scoped SQLite access.

% Contract

R1 (MUST): Explicit `path` always wins and preserves tests, migrations and one-off tools.
R2 (MUST): An omitted path resolves the active collection at call time, not import time, and falls back to legacy `DEFAULT_INDEX` when no registry exists.
R3 (MUST): All schema creation/additive migrations apply equally to legacy and per-volume databases.
R4 (MUST): Existing callers using `connect()` immediately follow a live collection switch without process restart.
R5 (MUST NOT): Never mutate the registry from `connect`, and never silently fall back to another database when a registered active collection is unavailable.
R6 (MUST NOT): Never merge collection rows, scan roots or enrichment caches across databases.
R7 (MUST): Keep the existing absolute-path track primary key and all current schema/data-preservation behavior.
R8 (MUST): Migrate scan_state.scan_pid additively; begin_scan records its process. A status-only open of an existing schema must not mark required migrations complete.
R9 (MUST): Recover a running row with a dead owner; a current-process owner may be recovered only when the editor explicitly reports no active scan thread. Never clear an active thread or a live foreign PID.
R10 (MUST): A legacy row without PID may recover only with explicit idle-editor context, a finite positive started_at older than this editor, and open-file ownership proving only this editor holds the database. Missing lsof, timeouts, unknown ownership, another holder or a recent/unknown start must preserve it. Old scanners retain an open database throughout discovery and reading, including custom harnesses.
R11 (MUST): Recovery updates only the scan-state row, preserving counters, warnings, tracks, notes, roots and mix artifacts. Compare running/started_at/owner atomically so a competing new scan wins. Use a bounded write wait and retain busy state under writer contention. Record an interrupted message and finish timestamp, log the recovery, then report fresh state. It never starts a new scan.

% Output

- Primary output: `brain/library_index.py`.

% Verification

- Run active-resolution, explicit-path, missing-volume and cross-collection isolation tests, all existing collection/scan tests, full unittest, and py_compile.
